# Optional credentials for squad. ALL of this is optional: with no keys the loop still runs.
# Trello sync is skipped; Claude's @developer/@qa use the native Agent fallback; Codex already uses
# native subagents and does not need OpenRouter.
#
#   cp .env.example ~/.codex/squad.env    ← Codex
#   cp .env.example ~/.claude/squad.env   ← Claude Code
#   export SQUAD_ENV_FILE=/another/path   ← explicit shared override
#
# It lives outside the plugin on purpose: installed as a plugin, this repo sits in a cache directory
# that is replaced on every update, so a .env kept in here would be lost. Shell variables always
# win over this file.
#
# --- Trello: BOARD mirror (/squad:* in Claude, $squad:* in Codex) ---
#
# Where they come from: https://trello.com/power-ups/admin → your power-up → API key tab.
# CAREFUL: that page shows an "API Key" and a "Secret". THE SECRET DOES NOT GO HERE (it is for
# OAuth and this script never uses it). What goes here is:
#   TRELLO_KEY   = the API Key.
#   TRELLO_TOKEN = the TOKEN generated from the "Token" link next to the key (you authorize by
#                  hand and it gives you a long string).
TRELLO_KEY=
TRELLO_TOKEN=

# --- OpenRouter: optional Claude-only engine for @developer and @qa ---
#
# Key: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys — without it Claude uses its native Agent fallback.
# and carries on.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Optional — defaults to openai/gpt-5.6-sol:
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=
